{
  "message": "The good news is that the emulation recorded no failures, and the design is intact: all eight blockers are \"implementation needed\" or \"existing system reference needed\" gaps, not design faults. The real issue is that the only Azure contract the product can generate today is private Blob Storage, so Event Hubs, the redaction Functions, AI Search, the Durable orchestrator and Azure OpenAI each need new generator and runtime code first. A graph edit can't fix that, and swapping in storage-only would cut the scope you asked for, so I'm not proposing a change; this is a product engineering task, and this run (artifact 7f2ea47b…, revision 2) is the reproducer. While that work is scheduled, which country do the synthetic logs and triage data need to stay in?",
